with Apollo for AI chip financing\n10/26/2026 6:07am\nSpaceX said on Monday an affiliate of Apollo ​Global Management will buy AI chips and server hardware and lease them to the ‌rockets-to-AI firm, in a deal with total principal payments of ⁠about $40 billion.\n# India's Tata Communications to spend $450 million on AI connectivity infrastructure\n10/26/2026 2:32am\nTata Communications, which ​offers data connections and cybersecurity to enterprises, ‌announced investments of close to $450 ⁠million on ​Monday to ⁠build high-speed network ‌cables connecting ‌India's AI data-centre corridors.","source":"web","title":"Browse by Day Archive | 2026/10/26","url":"https://www.ksl.com/archive/2026/10/26/_news_utah_science-and-tech"},{"date":"2026-10-26","id":4,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"## Latest Stories\n#### Voices: Eight hours after being in crisis, I was expected to return to normal life. We need better mental health support.\nBy Emilee Swensen | For The Salt Lake Tribune | October 26, 2026, 12:05 p.m.\n#### For all the damage Israel has meted out against its enemies, the Iranian regime stands. Hezbollah stands. Hamas stands. And America’s special relationship with Israel is drawing to its end.\nBy Ezra Klein | The New York Times | October 26, 2026, 12:01 p.m.\n#### Heavy rain in southeast Utah has prompted a rise in Lake Powell’s water level. Here’s how much.\n#### “It’s a nice start to the water year,” says a hydrologist, though the increase doesn’t solve the lake’s drought problems.\nBy Sean P. Means | October 26, 2026, 12:00 p.m.\n#### Letter: I’ve seen Yugoslavia under Tito’s imperious gaze and America under Trump’s. Vote.\nBy Mary O'Brien | The Public Forum | October 26, 2026, 12:00 p.m.\n#### ‘He’s our guy’: How Devon Dampier willed Utah football to a win over Houston\n#### Dampier accounted for roughly 82% of Utah’s total yardage against Houston.\nBy Jason Batacao | October 26, 2026, 12:00 p.m.\n#### Opinion: Everything feels so expensive. Here’s what’s really going on.\n#### Whatever you call it, we can all agree this doesn’t feel good.\nBy Natasha Sarin | For The New York Times | October 26, 2026, 12:00 p.m.\n#### The Jazz didn’t need a Walker Kessler revenge game to learn a lesson in loss to the Lakers\n#### Walker Kessler’s quiet return couldn’t hide the Jazz’s growing pains.\nBy Shreyas Laddha | October 26, 2026, 12:00 p.m.\n#### Here’s what’s happening this week, Oct. 26-Nov. 1, in southern Utah\n#### Everything from entertainment to recreation across southern Utah.\nBy Anthony Solis | October 26, 2026, 12:00 p.m.\n#### Utah lawmakers know prisoners can wait years for a public defender to file their appeal. They haven’t increased funding.\n#### “It’s crushing,” one former public defender says of the backlog, which leaves prisoners waiting for legal help and victims waiting for resolution.\nBy Robert Gehrke | Jessica Schreifels | October 26, 2026, 12:00 p.m.\n#### Utah is one of the best states for business — but most are run by men. This free 15-week program aims to change that.\n#### Applications are due Oct. 30.\nBy Paighten Harkins | October 26, 2026, 12:00 p.m.\n#### Utahns have sticker shock. Riley Owen and Ben McAdams have plans to help.\n#### The candidates for Utah’s 1st Congressional District agree voters are worried about expenses, but they differ on the cure.\nBy Robert Gehrke | October 26, 2026, 12:00 p.m.\n#### Bird flu is raging on a Utah mink farm. It could spark a human pandemic, experts say, but officials won’t act.\n#### Federal officials brushed off the issue as Utah prioritized the fur industry’s interests. Little has been done to stop the spread of the virus and ensure it can’t spread to humans, a failure that experts called “irresponsible” and “astounding.”\nBy Nat Lash | ProPublica and Julie Leopo | For ProPublica | October 26, 2026, 12:00 p.m.\n#### Southern Utah is turning away millions in convention business. Washington County has a $30M idea to change that.\n#### Officials say tourists, not taxpayers, will foot the bill for the $30 million project.\nBy Mark Eddington | October 26, 2026, 12:00 p.m.\n#### Jana Riess: The key message of the LDS Church’s new visitors’ center? We’re Christian, darn it.\n#### The center also aims to demystify the temple.\nBy Jana Riess | Religion News Service | October 26, 2026, 12:00 p.m.","source":"web","title":"Latest - The Salt Lake Tribune","url":"https://www.sltrib.com/latest/"},{"date":"2026-10-26","id":5,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"Salt Lake City News, Weather, Sports, Breaking News\nEmergency shelter opened as flooding forces evacuations in Four Corners area\nAn emergency shelter was opened at San Juan High School in Blanding after evacuations were ordered for the Four Corners region.The evacuations were ordered fo\nHeavy rain floods Four Corners as San Juan River nears historic crest\nHeavy rain caused serious flooding in the Four Corners region, and weather experts said the situation might still get worse.Sunday night, San Juan County offici\nUtah warms Monday before cool front brings showers to northern Utah\nShowers have come to an end across eastern Utah.\nTemperatures will get a big boost heading into Monday.\nThe Wasatch Front will reach the mid-60s with dry skies.\nMore flooding in Four Corners region after storms bring rain and at least one tornado\n...\nA man was shot and killed during an incident with police near a hotel in West Valley City.Officers with the West Valley City Police Department were called to th\n...\nLuka Doncic scored 52 points, hitting eight 3-pointers, to lead the Los Angeles Lakers to a 132-123 victory over the Utah Jazz on Sunday.In the first 50-point g\nNavajo Nation communities evacuated in Utah due to potential for 'catastrophic flooding'\nSeveral Navajo Nation communities in Utah were ordered to evacuate due to the potential for \"catastrophic flooding\" in the Four Corners region.The Navajo Police\nPHOTOS: Repeated flooding leaves widespread damage across Southern Utah\nSouthern Utah experienced severe flooding over the past week, and for eastern communities the flood danger is not over yet.More than a hundred homes were damage\nSalt Lake City International Airport celebrates completion of 12-year construction project\nSalt Lake City International Airport marked the end of its 12-year redevelopment project with a ceremony Saturday night featuring new music and an art installat\n...\nCold front brings rain, mountain snow to Utah before Halloween weekend\n## Local News\nBundle up tonight as skies clear and temperatures drop into the low 40s along the Wasatch Front and below freezing in the Wasatch Back.Showers will continue ov\nTexas State tops Utah State 20-17 on Jacob Bonilla's field goal late in fourth quarter\n...\nCedar City lifts boil order after follow-up water tests come back negative for E. coli","source":"web","title":"Salt Lake City News, Weather, Sports, Breaking News","url":"https://kutv.com/"},{"date":"2026-10-26","id":6,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"Annual Kirkin' o' th' Tartan' concludes 40th Scottish Festival\n...\n# Annual Kirkin' o' th' Tartan' concludes 40th Scottish Festival\nKTVX Salt Lake City\nMon, October 26, 2026 at 1:58 AM UTC\n...\nThe First Presbyterian Church of Salt Lake City celebrated the 40th Anniversary of its Scottish Festival with a traditional Kirkin' o' th' Tartan' worship service.","source":"web","title":"Annual Kirkin' o' th' Tartan' concludes 40th Scottish Festival","url":"https://www.yahoo.com/news/videos/annual-kirkin-o-th-tartan-015839357.html"},{"date":"2026-10-25","id":7,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"### SLC Council votes to preserve green space at Ballpark site after input from residents\n...\n## News\n### Navajo Nation communities ordered to evacuate ahead of expected flooding","source":"web","title":"The Salt Lake Tribune - Utah News, Sports, Religion \u0026 Entertainment","url":"https://www.sltrib.com/"},{"date":"2026-10-26","id":8,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"University of Utah holds soapbox derby for homecoming\n...\n# University of Utah holds soapbox derby for homecoming\nKTVX Salt Lake City\nMon, October 26, 2026 at 2:06 AM UTC\n...\nThe University of Utah held a soapbox derby for homecoming week, with teams comprised of six members competing.","source":"web","title":"University of Utah holds soapbox derby for homecoming","url":"https://www.yahoo.com/news/videos/university-utah-holds-soapbox-derby-020634783.html"},{"date":"2026-10-26","id":9,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"Salt Lake City Library Wi-Fi CSAM Arrest: Perea Charged\nMonday, October 26, 2026Set Location\n...\n# Salt Lake City Library Wi-Fi CSAM Arrest: Perea Charged\n...\nAdrian Mathias Perea, on federal probation for child porn, faces 10 felony counts after CSAM was traced to Salt Lake City library Wi-Fi.","source":"web","title":"Salt Lake City Library Wi-Fi CSAM Arrest: Perea Charged","url":"https://ground.news/article/salt-lake-city-library-wi-fi-csam-arrest-perea-charged"},{"date":"2026-10-26","id":10,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"With ‘major events’ looming, LDS Church partners with Department of Homeland Security on safety\nMonday, October 26, 2026Set Location\nPublished 24 days ago • loading...\n• Updated 24 days ago\n# With ‘major events’ looming, LDS Church partners with Department of Homeland Security on safety\n...\nFederal authorities are helping to beef up the LDS Church’s security ahead of “major events.\"\nThe faith hosts General Conference this weekend and a six-month open house for the renovated Salt Lake Temple next year.","source":"web","title":"With ‘major events’ looming, LDS Church partners with Department of Homeland Security on safety","url":"https://ground.news/article/with-major-events-looming-lds-church-partners-with-department-of-homeland-security-on-safety"},{"date":"2026-10-26","id":11,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"New documentary spotlights Great Salt Lake decline, potential health risks\nMonday, October 26, 2026Set Location\n...\n# New documentary spotlights Great Salt Lake decline, potential health risks\n...\nA new documentary putting the Great Salt Lake’s decline under the spotlight is drawing crowds to downtown Salt Lake City.\nFree screenings are giving Utahns a chance to learn more about the issue.","source":"web","title":"New documentary spotlights Great Salt Lake decline, potential health risks","url":"https://ground.news/article/new-documentary-spotlights-great-salt-lake-decline-potential-health-risks"},{"date":"2026-10-26","id":12,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"# Grizzlies play the Jazz, aim for 4th straight win\nBy\nTHE ASSOCIATED PRESS\nUpdated 6:02 AM UTC, October 26, 2026\nMemphis Grizzlies (3-0, fourth in the Western Conference) vs. Utah Jazz (1-2, 12th in the Western Conference)\nSalt Lake City; Monday, 9 p.m.\nEDT\nLINE: Jazz -1.5; over/under is 238.5\nBOTTOM LINE: Memphis is looking to keep its three-game win streak alive when the Grizzlies take on Utah.\n...\nThe two teams match up for the second time this season.\nThe Grizzlies defeated the Jazz 123-103 in their last meeting on Oct. 22. Ty Jerome led the Grizzlies with 45 points, and Keyonte George led the Jazz with 22 points.\nINJURIES: Jazz: Jusuf Nurkic: out (foot).\nGrizzlies: Zach Edey: out ().","source":"web","title":"Grizzlies play the Jazz, aim for 4th straight win","url":"https://apnews.com/article/memphis-grizzlies-utah-jazz-utah-memphis-5d286dee2f604d6cb404d088e41d8f1f"},{"id":13,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"## Salt Lake County prosecutors using AI to review evidence; DA says humans remain in control\n## As prosecutors from across the country gather in Salt Lake City, officials are sharing how artificial intelligence is changing criminal investigations — and why they say safeguards are essential.\n...\n## Navajo Nation, San Juan County communities ordered to evacuate due to potential flooding\n...\n## Eric Bauza, voice actor behind Bugs Bunny and other Looney Tunes stars, dies at 46\n#### Laura Sharman, CNN | Updated Oct. 26 - 7:17 a.m. | Save Story\n##### Eric Bauza, the voice actor behind the modern-day Bugs Bunny and Daffy Duck, among other iconic animated characters, has died at age 46, according to his family and official health records.\n## Where Salt Lake City, Delta Center and Jazz Bear rank among NBA fans\n#### Video Dennis Romboy, Deseret News | Posted Oct. 26 - 7:09 a.m. | Save Story\n##### When the Utah Jazz host the New Orleans Pelicans in their home opener Friday night, Salt Lake City will be hoppin', Delta Center will be rockin', and Bear will be boppin'.","source":"web","title":"Utah Breaking News, Top Stories \u0026 Sports | World, US, Local","url":"https://www.ksl.com/"},{"date":"2026-10-26","id":14,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"Browse by Day Archive | 2026/10/26 | KSL.com","source":"web","title":"Browse by Day Archive | 2026/10/26 | KSL.com","url":"https://www.ksl.com/archive/2026/10/26/_news_features_lifestyle"},{"date":"2026-10-15","id":15,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"Salt Lake City Diocese hopes to start something new with lay ministry for OCIA - OSV News\nMonday, October 26, 2026\n...\n# Salt Lake City Diocese hopes to start something new with lay ministry for OCIA\n(OSV News photo/Marie Mischel, Intermountain Catholic)\n*676*\n(OSV News) — The Diocese of Salt Lake City is initiating a new lay ministry role of “Worthy and Suitable Catechists” who can administer minor rites to those joining or completing their initiation into the Catholic Church.\n...\nValdez is one of 31 Worthy and Suitable Catechists recently commissioned by Bishop Oscar A. Solis of Salt Lake City to impart some of the minor rites of the Order of Christian Initiation of Adults, also known as OCIA.","source":"web","title":"Salt Lake City Diocese hopes to start something new with lay ministry for OCIA","url":"https://www.osvnews.com/salt-lake-city-diocese-hopes-to-start-something-new-with-lay-ministry-for-ocia/"}],"type":"search_results"},"output_index":0,"sequence_number":9,"type":"response.output_item.done"}

