soula|DL4112|On Time|A42|\n|1:33 PM|Omaha|DL3896|On Time|A2|\n|10:56 PM|Oakland|DL3797|On Time|A28|\n|3:19 PM|Oakland|DL3903|On Time|A49|","source":"web","title":"Search Arrivals and Departures - Salt Lake City","url":"https://slcairport.com/airlines-flights/arrivals-departures?type=simple\u0026search_flight=\u0026query_leg=D\u0026sortby=destination\u0026sortdir=asc\u0026page=16\u0026results_per_page=20\u0026query_flight=\u0026query_date1=\u0026query_date2=\u0026query_city=\u0026query_gate=\u0026query_airline="},{"date":"2026-10-13","id":39,"last_updated":"2026-10-21","snippet":"## Tagged ‘Salt Lake City Council’\n#### October 6, 2026 Meeting Recap\nThe Council approved emergency assistance for Poplar Grove families affected by flooding, updated Public Utilities impact fees, and heard public comment on several land use and property proposals.","source":"web","title":"Salt Lake City Council - SLC.gov","url":"https://www.slc.gov/council/tag/salt-lake-city-council/"},{"id":40,"last_updated":"2026-10-23","snippet":"## Latest News\n#### Madsen Park to temporarily close for upgrades\n*Posted on:* October 22nd, 2026\nOct. 22, 2026 Salt Lake City’s Department of Public Lands will temporarily close Madsen Park (9 N.\nChicago St.) on October 26, 2026, to begin construction on a series of new amenities prioritized by residents and designed to celebrate the community this park serves.\nThe park is scheduled to reopen in Spring 2027.","source":"web","title":"SLC.gov","url":"https://www.slc.gov/"},{"date":"2026-10-13","id":41,"last_updated":"2026-10-22","snippet":"*Posted on:* October 21st, 2026\nThe Council approved new zoning regulations as part of the Ballpark NEXT plan, discussed discussed potential alterations to the Expanding Housing Options proposal, and more.","source":"web","title":"Meeting Recaps | City Council Office","url":"https://www.slc.gov/council/category/news/meeting-recaps/"},{"id":42,"last_updated":"2026-10-25","snippet":"## Tagged ‘Salt Lake City Council’\n#### Madsen Park to temporarily close for upgrades\n...\nOct. 22, 2026 Salt Lake City’s Department of Public Lands will temporarily close Madsen Park (9 N.\nChicago St.) on October 26, 2026, to begin construction on a series of new amenities prioritized by residents and designed to celebrate the community this park serves.\nThe park is scheduled to reopen in Spring 2027.","source":"web","title":"Tagged 'Salt Lake City Council'","url":"https://www.slc.gov/blog/tag/salt-lake-city-council/"},{"date":"2026-10-24","id":43,"last_updated":"2026-10-25","snippet":"### Oct 24 2026 SLC International Celebrates Completion of Construction with a Musical Premiere\nSalt Lake City Department of Airports has achieved something not done this century: constructed the first new hub airport in the United States.\nTo celebrate this milestone, SLCDA commissioned Utah composer Kurt Bestor to write an airport theme to celebrate flight.\n...\n### Oct 24 2026 Touch Down: SLC International Airport Celebrates the End of an Era\nWith the wave of a composer’s baton, the Salt Lake City International Airport celebrated the end The New SLC Redevelopment Program—a 12-year construction project—on Saturday night.\nThe theme for the celebration was “Gateway to the World,” highlighting the airport’s transformation to a global facility.\n...\n### Oct 24 2026 Art Installations Create a Sense of Place in The New SLC Airport\nSalt Lake City Department of Airports marked the completion of The New SLC on Oct. 23 by unveiling “Crossroads to the World,” a suspended installation of about 2,500 colorful, laser-cut acrylic airplanes—the final art piece in the airport’s 12-year rebuild.","source":"web","title":"2026 | Salt Lake City International Airport","url":"https://slcairport.com/pressroom/news-releases/2026/"},{"date":"2026-10-07","id":44,"last_updated":"2026-10-22","snippet":"- ## Salt Lake City Public Utilities Impact Fees\nOctober 7, 2026\nOn Tuesday, Oct. 6, 2026, the Salt Lake City Council approved updates to existing water, sewer and stormwater impact fees.\nThese one-time fees help pay for infrastructure needed to serve new development and are based on the principle that growth should help pay for growth.","source":"web","title":"Recently Completed Projects | City Council Office","url":"https://www.slc.gov/council/current-proposals/recently-completed-projects/"},{"id":45,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"1. Salt Lake County\n2. Executive Coordinating Committee\n3. October Executive Coordinating Committee Meeting\n# October Executive Coordinating Committee Meeting\n...\n### General Information\n...\nCounty\n- **Entity**\nSalt Lake County\n- **Public Body**\nExecutive Coordinating Committee\n...\n- **Notice Title**\nOctober Executive Coordinating Committee Meeting\n- **Notice Type(s)**\nNotice\n- **Event Start Date \u0026 Time**\nOctober 26, 2026 01:30 PM\n- **Event End Date \u0026 Time**\nOctober 26, 2026 03:00 PM\n- **Event Deadline Date \u0026 Time**\n10/26/26 01:30 PM\n- **Description/Agenda**\n1.\nCALL TO ORDER 2.\nPUBLIC COMMENT 3.\nAPPROVAL OF MINUTES 3.1 September 28, 2026 Meeting Minutes 26-1095 Presenter: Andrea De Paz - Senior Administrator \u0026 Council Liaison Discussion - Vote Needed Attachments: 1. September ECC Meeting Minutes 9.28.26 4.\nDISCUSSION ITEMS 4.1 ADA Web Compliance Update 26-1083 Presenter: Kelly Deleon, ADA/Employee Relations Coordinator (15 minutes) Informational Attachments: 1.\nADA Web Compliance Presentation 4.2 SLCO Subsidies Related to Medicare Supplement Plan Premiums 26-1088 Presenter: David Delquadro (5 minutes) Informational Attachments: 1.\nDRAFT Medicare Supplement Policy Change 2026 Oct. 22 Executive Coordinating Committee Meeting Agenda October 26, 2026 5.\nSTANDING UPDATES 5.1 Privacy Program and Smart Gov Fund Update 26-1089 Presenter: Javaid Lal - Director of Performance \u0026 Innovation (10 Minutes) Informational Attachments: None 5.1 Privacy Program Update - Presentation 26-1093 Presenter: Javaid Lal - Director of Performance and \u0026 Innovation (5 Minutes) Informational Attachments: 1.\nSLCo_ECC_Privacy_Program_Update Oct 2026 5.1 Salt Lake County Policy on Personal Data Privacy 26-1094 Presenter: Javaid Lal - Director of Performance and Innovation (10 minutes) Discussion - Vote Needed Attachments: 1.\nSLCo_Policy_2022_Proposed_Changes_2026 5.2 TAB Update 26-1090 Presenter: Tony Jolley - CIO (Less than 5 Minutes) Informational Attachments: None 5.3 HR Update 26-1091 Presenter: Sharon Roux - Director of Human Resources (Less than 5 Minutes) Executive Coordinating Committee Meeting Agenda October 26, 2026 Attachments: None 5.4 New Campus Update 26-1092 Presenter: Megan Hillyard - Director of Administrative Services (Less than 5 Minutes) Attachments: None 6.\n...\n- **Meeting Location**\n2001 S.\nState Street N2-800 Salt Lake City, UT 84190 Show in Apple Maps Show in Google Maps\n...\nElise Courtney\n...\nOctober 23, 2026 03:55 PM\n...\n- **Deadline Date**\nOctober 26, 2026 01:30 PM\n...\n|File Name|Category|Date Added|\n|--|--|--|\n|Executive Coordinating Committee - 10.26.2026 Agenda.pdf|Other|2026/10/23 03:54 PM|","source":"web","title":"Notice","url":"https://www.utah.gov/pmn/sitemap/notice/1118041.html"}],"type":"search_results"},{"queries":["Salt Lake City events Monday October 26 2026","Utah Jazz October 26 2026 Salt Lake City","Salt Lake City concert October 26 2026"],"results":[{"date":"2026-10-26","id":46,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"# Treat Your Shelf Book Club\nSalt Lake City Public Library Main Branch\n210 East 400 South, Salt Lake City\nOct 26, 2026 at 6:00pm\nA new book club for adults!\nMake friends, have a snack, and read and discuss a new book each month.\nClick for the book schedule!\nCopies of the next month’s book will be given out at each meeting.\nReading Schedule\n**Monday, October 26, 6-7:30pm · Educated by Tara Westover** **Mo**\n...\n## Treat Your Shelf Book Club\nSalt Lake City Public Library Main Branch\nSalt Lake City | 6:00pm","source":"web","title":"Treat Your Shelf Book Club","url":"https://www.ksl.com/events/details/604819?date=2026-10-26"},{"date":"2026-10-26","id":47,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"1. Bright Star\n# Bright Star\nTerrace Plaza Playhouse\n99 East 4700 South, Ogden\nOct 26, 2026 at 7:30pmSee Additional Dates\nBright Star is a heartfelt, bluegrass-infused musical about love, hope, and the surprising connections that can change the course of a life.\n...\n## Ticket Information\nSECTION A\nAdults $25\nSenior (62+)/Students $24\nMilitary $24\nChild (12 \u0026 under) $20\n(please no babes in arms)\nSECTIONS B \u0026 C\nAdults $23\nSenior(62+)/Students $22\nMilitary $22\nChild (12 \u0026 under) $18\n(please no babes in arms)\nBox Office Hours\n...\n6:00-7:00pm (Mon, Fri, Sat)\n6:00-8:00pm (Wed)\n...\n## Bright Star\nTerrace Plaza Playhouse\nOgden | 7:30pm","source":"web","title":"Bright Star","url":"https://www.ksl.com/events/details/602057?date=2026-10-26"},{"date":"2026-10-26","id":48,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"# Dinosaur Jr live at The Complex\nThe Complex\n536 West 100 South, Salt Lake City\nOct 26, 2026 at 7:00pm\nDinosaur Jr. bring the Fall Tour 2026 to The Complex on October 26th, 2026!\nS\u0026S Presents\nDinosaur Jr.\nWith Special Guest: Stef Chura\nMonday, October 26 Doors 7:00PM, Show 8:00PM All Ages","source":"web","title":"Dinosaur Jr live at The Complex","url":"https://www.ksl.com/events/details/592565?date=2026-10-26"},{"date":"2026-10-26","id":49,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"# 3D Design and Print Workshop\nSalt Lake City Public Library Glendale Branch\n1375 South Concord, Salt Lake City\nOct 26, 2026 at 3:00pmSee Additional Dates\nBilingual 3D design and printing workshop for kids age 10+.\nEach Monday, Oct 5–Nov 9.\nTaller bilingüe de diseño e impresión 3D para niños de 10 años en adelante.\nCada lunes, del 5 de oct – 9 de nov.\n...\nOct26\n## 3D Design and Print Workshop\nSalt Lake City Public Library Glendale Branch\nSalt Lake City | 3:00pm\nLearn More\nOct26\n## Disability in Horror Films Lecture by Angela Smith\nSalt Lake City Public Library Marmalade Branch\nSalt Lake City | 6:30pm","source":"web","title":"3D Design and Print Workshop","url":"https://www.ksl.com/events/details/604795?date=2026-10-26"},{"date":"2026-10-26","id":50,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"1. Daily Organ Recitals on Temple Square\n# Daily Organ Recitals on Temple Square\nTabernacle on Temple Square\n50 West North Temple, Salt Lake City\nOct 26, 2026 at 12:00pmSee Additional Dates\nThe world famous organs on Temple Square are featured in daily concerts played by members of the organ staff and volunteer organists.\nFor over a century, visitors to Temple Square have been able to enjoy daily recitals featuring the famous pipe organs in the Tabernacle\n## Ticket Information\nFree Admission\n...\n## Sunday Organ Recitals on Temple Square\nOct26\n## Daily Organ Recitals on Temple Square\nTabernacle on Temple Square\nSalt Lake City | 12:00pm","source":"web","title":"Daily Organ Recitals on Temple Square","url":"https://www.ksl.com/events/details/562687?date=2026-10-26"},{"date":"2026-10-26","id":51,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"1. Little Shop of Horrors\n# Little Shop of Horrors\nSimmons Pioneer Memorial Theatre - University of Utah\n300 South 1400 East, Salt Lake City\nOct 26, 2026 at 7:00pmSee Additional Dates\n...\n## Ticket Information\nMain Floor/Loge: $89\nBalcony: $62\n...\n## Similar Events\nOct26\n## Little Shop of Horrors\nSimmons Pioneer Memorial Theatre - University of Utah\nSalt Lake City | 7:00pm","source":"web","title":"Little Shop of Horrors","url":"https://www.ksl.com/events/details/573632?date=2026-10-26"},{"date":"2026-10-26","id":52,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"# The Halloween Express 2026\nHeber Valley Railroad\n450 South 600 West, Heber City\nOct 26, 2026 at 7:00pmSee Additional Dates\nJoin on this Halloween journey to the haunted Grim Hollow station.\nOn board you will be entertained by our hosts and a cast of characters!\nThis is a 90 minute family-friendly train experience.\nThe Halloween Express runs on Monday, Thursday, and Friday evenings throughout October.\n...\n## Ticket Information\n$35 - General Admission, ages 2+.\nYou'll ride in one of our standard historic coaches.\n...\n## The Halloween Express 2026\nHeber Valley Railroad\nHeber City | 7:00pm\n...\nOct26\n## Ken Ludwig's Moriarty\nSorensen Legacy Jewel Box Stage\nSandy | 7:00pm","source":"web","title":"The Halloween Express 2026","url":"https://www.ksl.com/events/details/593989?date=2026-10-26"},{"date":"2026-10-26","id":53,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"# Grizzlies play the Jazz, aim for 4th straight win\n...\nUpdated 6:02 AM UTC, October 26, 2026\nMemphis Grizzlies (3-0, fourth in the Western Conference) vs. Utah Jazz (1-2, 12th in the Western Conference)\nSalt Lake City; Monday, 9 p.m.\nEDT\nLINE: Jazz -1.5; over/under is 238.5\n...\nThe two teams match up for the second time this season.\nThe Grizzlies defeated the Jazz 123-103 in their last meeting on Oct. 22. Ty Jerome led the Grizzlies with 45 points, and Keyonte George led the Jazz with 22 points.\nINJURIES: Jazz: Jusuf Nurkic: out (foot).","source":"web","title":"Grizzlies play the Jazz, aim for 4th straight win","url":"https://apnews.com/article/memphis-grizzlies-utah-jazz-utah-memphis-5d286dee2f604d6cb404d088e41d8f1f"},{"date":"2026-10-26","id":54,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"# Utah Jazz vs. Memphis Grizzlies\nDelta Center\n301 South Temple, Salt Lake City\nOct 26, 2026 at 7:00pm\nBe a part of the action as the Utah Jazz play at the Delta Center in Salt Lake City.\n...\n## Similar Events\nOct26\n## Utah Jazz vs. Memphis Grizzlies\nDelta Center\nSalt Lake City | 7:00pm","source":"web","title":"Utah Jazz vs. Memphis Grizzlies","url":"https://www.ksl.com/events/details/598339?date=2026-10-26"},{"date":"2026-10-26","id":55,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"# Events for October 26, 2026\n## 6:00 pm\n### Full Moon Walk- EKO\nOctober 26 @ 6:15 pm - 7:45 pm\nWillard Bay State Park, 900 W 650 N, Willard, UT 84340, USA\nExperience the park by moonlight on a park ranger naturalist led walk along the beach, nature trail, and campgrounds of Willard Bay State Park.\nDress for the weather and wear close toed shoes.\nNo flashlights please.\nEvent is free with paid park entry or Utah State Parks Annual PassWhere: Willard Bay General Store\n1594 West North Temple\nSalt Lake City, UT 84116\nHours: Monday - Friday, 8:00 am - 5:00 pm\nPhone: 801-538-7220","source":"web","title":"Events for October 26, 2026","url":"https://stateparks.utah.gov/events/today/"},{"date":"2026-10-26","id":56,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"# Expressions of the Soul Art Show\nRed Cliff Gallery\n220 N 200 E, Saint George\nOct 26, 2026 at 9:00amSee Additional Dates\nExpressions of the Soul art show\nEXHIBITION OPEN TO PUBLIC\nFriday, September 11 through Thursday, October 29, Monday through Friday 9 am to 5 pm and Saturdays Noon to 4 pm at Red Cliff Gallery.\n...\n## Parking Information\nFree Parking next to the Commons Building","source":"web","title":"Expressions of the Soul Art Show","url":"https://www.ksl.com/events/details/593464?date=2026-10-26"},{"date":"2026-10-25","id":57,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"# Concerts in Salt Lake City\n## All Salt Lake City Concerts\n- (opens in new tab) Find tickets from 52 dollars to Post Sex Nachos on Mon, Oct 26, 6:00pm at Kilby Court - Salt Lake City in Salt Lake City, UT\nOct 26\nMon · 6:00pm\nPost Sex Nachos\n$52·Kilby Court - Salt Lake City·Salt Lake City, UT\nFrom $52\n- (opens in new tab) Find tickets from 48 dollars to New Constellations with Vox Rea on Mon, Oct 26, 8:00pm at Soundwell in Salt Lake City, UT\nOct 26\nMon · 8:00pm\nNew Constellations with Vox Rea\n$48·Soundwell·Salt Lake City, UT\nFrom $48\n- (opens in new tab) Find tickets from 59 dollars to Dinosaur Jr. with Stef Chura on Mon, Oct 26, 8:00pm at Rockwell At The Complex in Salt Lake City, UT\nOct 26\nMon · 8:00pm\nDinosaur Jr. with Stef Chura\n$59·Rockwell At The Complex·Salt Lake City, UT","source":"web","title":"Salt Lake City Concert Calendar \u0026 Tickets 2026-2027 | SeatGeek","url":"https://seatgeek.com/cities/salt-lake-city/concerts"},{"date":"2023-02-15","id":58,"last_updated":"2026-10-23","snippet":"## Monday, October 26\n### Wheeler Farm Pumpkin Days\n10:00 AM—8:00 PM\nWheeler Historic Farm, 6351 S 900 E, Murray, UT 84121\nwheelerfarm@saltlakecounty.gov\nOther Languages: No\n**Neighborhood:** County Wide, Murray\nWheelchair Access\n...\n- **Dates**: September 25-October 31\n- **Hours**: Monday-Thursday, 10 am-8 pm | Fri-Sat, 9 am-9 pm | Sun, 9 am-4 pm\n- **Location**: North Parking Lot Pasture\n**Wagons, Cow Trains \u0026 Country Store**-  **Hours**: Open daily during Pumpkin Patch hours.\n...\n- **Friday–Saturday:** 9 am–9 pm\n- **Sunday:** 9 am–4 pm\nExpanded Daytime Hours (10 am–8 pm)- **UEA Break:** Thursday, Oct 15 \u0026 Oct 22\n- **Monday Fun:** Oct 19 \u0026 Oct 26\nHalloween Hours (Oct 31)- 10 am–4 pm\nAdmission \u0026 Pricing- **Pumpkin Days Ticket:** $12 (Includes maze, playland, and one ride)\n…\n### Boos, Beats and High Fitness | Sorenson Multi-Cultural Center\n5:30 PM—6:30 PM\n*855 California Ave, Salt Lake City, UT 84104*\nOther Languages: No\n**Neighborhood:** Salt Lake City\nJoin Sorenson Multi-Cultural Center and a special Halloween-themed High Fitness Class!\nFree with a Center or All County Recreation Membership or $6 to drop in!\n...\n### AstroTots\n10:30 AM—11:30 AM\nLearning Space at Clark Planetarium\n130 S 400 W\nSalt Lake City, UT 84101\n...\n### Clark After Dark: Escape the Space Station\n7:00 PM—10:00 PM\nClark Planetarium","source":"web","title":"Events Calendar | Salt Lake County","url":"https://www.saltlakecounty.gov/events-calendar/"},{"date":"2026-10-26","id":59,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"Dinosaur Jr.\n** Mon, 26 Oct 2026 ** The Grand at The Complex SLC - Complex\nTickets from $62\n...\n### Today, 26 October\nPop, Rock\nPost Sex Nachos\n** Mon, 26 Oct 2026 ** Kilby Court, Salt Lake City, UT\nTickets from $50\nRock, Indie \u0026 Alternative\nDinosaur Jr.\n** Mon, 26 Oct 2026 ** The Grand at The Complex SLC - Complex, Salt Lake City, UT\nTickets from $62\nPop, Indie \u0026 Alternative\nNew Constellations\n** Mon, 26 Oct 2026 ** Soundwell, Salt Lake City, UT\nTickets from $51","source":"web","title":"Concerts in Salt Lake City in October 2026: Tickets ...","url":"https://www.eventworld.com/salt-lake-city-ut/concerts/october"},{"id":60,"last_updated":"2026-10-13","snippet":"## 6:00 pm\n### Full Moon Walk- EKO\nOctober 26 @ 6:15 pm - 7:45 pm\nWillard Bay State Park, 900 W 650 N, Willard, UT 84340, USA\nExperience the park by moonlight on a park ranger naturalist led walk along the beach, nature trail, and campgrounds of Willard Bay State Park.\nDress for the weather and wear close toed shoes.\nNo flashlights please.\nEvent is free with paid park entry or Utah State Parks Annual PassWhere: Willard Bay General Store\n1594 West North Temple\nSalt Lake City, UT 84116\nHours: Monday - Friday, 8:00 am - 5:00 pm\nPhone: 801-538-7220","source":"web","title":"Events for October 26, 2026","url":"https://stateparks.utah.gov/events/2026-10-26/"}],"type":"search_results"},{"queries":["man dies shot police West Valley City hotel October 26 2026 details","West Valley City police hotel outbuilding shooting October 25 2026"],"results":[{"date":"2026-10-25","id":76,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"# Man dies after being shot by police outside of West Valley City hotel, police say\n#### Posted - Oct. 25, 2026 at 12:11 p.m.\n...\n#### A man died after being shot by a police officer outside of a hotel in West Valley City on Sunday, police say. (Istvan Bartos, KSL)\n...\nWEST VALLEY CITY — A man died after being shot by a police officer outside of a hotel in West Valley City on Sunday morning, police say.\nThe shooting happened outside of Marriott's TownePlace Suites hotel at 5473 West High Market Dr., after hotel employees called to report a man who was found inside a hotel storage building, according to Deputy Communications Director for West Valley City Roxeanne Vainuku.\nEmployees told police the man was armed with a large stick and was threatening to shoot the employees.\nWhen officers responded, they said the man was holding a \"large metal rod,\" according to Vainuku.\n\"Within moments after that, the officer had called out on the radio and said he had deployed his pepper spray and just moments after that the call came through that shots had been fired,\" Vainuku said.\nOfficers immediately attempted life-saving measures; however, medical responders who also attempted life-saving measures pronounced the man to be deceased when they arrived.\nInitially, witnesses said the man had run at officers with two large metal objects before the shooting occurred, according to Vainuku.\nVainuku called the occurrence rare, saying officers have the responsibility to protect themselves and others.\n\"This is never how we would want a situation to come to an end, but at the same time, officers have a responsibility to protect the safety of the people around them and also to protect themselves from danger,\" Vainuku said.\nThe incident was still under investigation as the scene was processed by the West Jordan Police Department.\nVainuku said the officer who fired at the man was placed on administrative leave as the investigation continued.","source":"web","title":"Man dies after being shot by police outside of West Valley City hotel, police say","url":"https://www.ksl.com/article/51640813/man-dies-after-being-shot-by-police-outside-of-west-valley-city-hotel-police-say"},{"date":"2026-10-25","id":77,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"Man killed in police incident after hotel employees found him in West Valley outbuilding\n# Man killed in police incident after hotel employees found him in West Valley outbuilding\n...\nSun, October 25, 2026 at 12:22 PM\nUpdated Sun, October 25, 2026 at 9:49 PM\n...\nA man was shot and killed during an incident with police near a hotel in West Valley City on Oct. 25, 2026.\n(Photo: Leah Criscione, KUTV)\n...\nWEST VALLEY CITY, Utah (KUTV) — A man was shot and killed during an incident with police near a hotel in West Valley City.\nOfficers with the West Valley City Police Department were called to the TownePlace Suites near 5400 West High Market Drive Sunday morning.\nPolice said hotel employees had gone to an outbuilding used for storage when they found a man armed with a metal stick.\nEmployees said the man threatened to shoot them.\nOfficials said the employees backed away and called 911, and West Valley officers responded to the scene.\n\"An officer called out that the man was armed with a large metal rod.\nMoments later, the officer called out that he had deployed pepper spray, and just moments after that came a call that shots had been fired,\" West Valley officials said.\nLife-saving measures were attempted, but the man was declared deceased.\nAt this time, the suspect's name is unknown as police work to confirm his identity.\nThey do not know why he was in the outbuilding.\nWitnesses told investigators that the suspect appeared to charge the officer with metal objects in both hands.\nHowever, the investigation is ongoing and details remain limited at this time.\n...\n\"And in the thousands and thousands of incidents that we respond to every year, an officer-involved critical incident, or a shooting, is very, very rare.\"\nVainuku said that in the rare event that an officer-involved shooting occurs, the case is investigated \"very thoroughly and used as a training point.\"\nThe investigation into this incident is being led by the West Jordan Police Department, and the officer involved in the shooting was placed on administrative leave, following protocol.","source":"web","title":"Man killed in police incident after hotel employees found him in West Valley outbuilding","url":"https://kutv.com/news/local/man-killed-in-police-incident-after-hotel-employees-found-him-in-west-valley-outbuilding"},{"date":"2026-10-25","id":78,"last_updated":"2026-10-25","snippet":"WEST VALLEY CITY, Utah, Oct. 25, 2026 (Gephardt Daily) — A man who West Valley City Police say was armed with a large stick and threatening to shoot was fatally shot Sunday morning at an extended-stay hotel complex, Townehouse Suites by Marriott, a WVCPD statement says.\n'Officers were dispatched to the Towneplace Suites at 5473 W.\nHighmarket Dr. at about 8:45 am.\nEmployees of the hotel accessed an outbuilding used for storage \u0026 found a man inside.\n'They described the man as armed with a large stick and reported he was threatening to shoot them.'\nOfficers arrived and encountered the man, the police statement says.\n'An officer called out that the man was armed with a large metal rod.\nMoments later, the officer called out that he had deployed pepper spray, and just moments after that came a call that shots had been fired.\n'Officers immediately began lifesaving efforts.\nFire arrived \u0026 took over.\nUltimately, the suspect was pronounced deceased.\nWitnesses on the scene are being interviewed.\nWitnesses initially describe suspect as running at the officer with large metal objects in both hands.\n'A full investigation into this incident is underway.\nIt is being conducted by the West Jordan Police Department's protocol team.\nThe officer involved is on administrative leave as is standard procedure in an officer involved critical incident.'\nRoxeanne Vainuku, speaking for the WVCPD, later told reporter at the scene that witnesses said the man charged at the officer right before shots were fired, and at the time of the news conference, the dead man's identity had not been determined.\nGephardt Daily will share additional information as it is released.","source":"web","title":"Shots fired, suspect dead after WVCPD officers respond to man who allegedly threatened hotel staff","url":"https://gephardtdaily.com/local/shots-fired-suspect-dead-after-wvcpd-officers-respond-to-man-who-allegedly-threatened-hotel-staff/"},{"date":"2026-10-25","id":79,"last_updated":"2026-10-25","snippet":"# Man dies after being shot by police outside of West Valley City hotel, police say\n10/25/2026 12:11pm\nA man died on Sunday after being shot by a police officer outside of a hotel in West Valley City, police say.","source":"web","title":"Browse by Day Archive | 2026/10/25 | KSL.com","url":"https://www.ksl.com/archive/2026/10/25/_news_utah_police-and-courts"},{"date":"2026-10-25","id":80,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"# Man dies after being shot by police outside of West Valley City hotel, police say\n10/25/2026 12:11pm\nA man died on Sunday after being shot by a police officer outside of a hotel in West Valley City, police say.","source":"web","title":"Browse by Day Archive | 2026/10/25 | KSL.com","url":"https://www.ksl.com/archive/2026/10/25/_"},{"date":"2026-10-26","id":81,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"West Valley City man killed in police involved incident\n...\n# West Valley City man killed in police involved incident\nKTVX Salt Lake City\nMon, October 26, 2026 at 1:55 AM UTC\n...\nA man was shot and killed in a police incident near a hotel after he was found in a storage building.","source":"web","title":"West Valley City man killed in police involved incident","url":"https://www.yahoo.com/news/videos/west-valley-city-man-killed-015531563.html"},{"date":"2026-10-26","id":82,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"Man killed in police incident after hotel employees found him in West Valley outbuilding\nA man was shot and killed during an incident with police near a hotel in West Valley City.Officers with the West Valley City Police Department were called to th\n...\nMan killed in police incident after hotel employees found him in West Valley outbuilding\nA man was shot and killed during an incident with police near a hotel in West Valley City.Officers with the West Valley City Police Department were called to th","source":"web","title":"Salt Lake City News, Weather, Sports, Breaking News","url":"https://kutv.com/"},{"date":"2026-10-20","id":83,"last_updated":"2026-10-25","snippet":"### Suspect fatally shot Sunday morning at West Valley City hotel\nA man was fatally shot by West Valley City Police on Sunday morning at the Towneplace Suites after allegedly threatening hotel staff with a large metal rod.\nWest Valley CityOctober 25, 2026\n...\n### Man killed in police incident after hotel employees found him in West Valley outbuilding\nA man was shot and killed during an incident with police near a hotel in West Valley City.\nOfficers with the West Valley City Police Department were called to the Townplace Suites near 5400 West High Market Drive Sunday morning.\nPolice said hotel employees had gone to an outbuilding on the property when they found a \"threatening\" man armed with a metal stick.\nvia KUTVWest Valley CityOctober 25, 2026","source":"web","title":"How the boring, monotonous work is paying off for the Utah Jazz's Ace Bailey","url":"https://utah.news/article/6AB87D05-0FA6-42BA-A379-FA49157D2F3E"},{"date":"2026-10-25","id":84,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"## West Valley City, UT · LATEST NEWS\n### Man dies after being shot by police outside of West Valley City hotel, police say\nWEST VALLEY CITY — A man died after being shot by a police officer outside of a hotel in West Valley City on Sunday morning, police say.\nThe shooting happened outside of Marriott's TownePlace Suites hotel at 5473 West High Market Dr., after hotel employees called to report a man who was found inside a hotel storage building, according to Deputy Communications Director for West Valley City Roxeanne Vainuku.","source":"web","title":"West Valley City, UT Local News and More | NewsBreak","url":"https://www.newsbreak.com/west-valley-city-ut"},{"date":"2026-10-21","id":85,"last_updated":"2026-10-25","snippet":"### Suspect fatally shot Sunday morning at West Valley City hotel\nA man was fatally shot by West Valley City Police on Sunday morning at the Towneplace Suites after allegedly threatening hotel staff with a large metal rod.\nWest Valley CityOctober 25, 2026\n...\n### Man killed in police incident after hotel employees found him in West Valley outbuilding\nA man was shot and killed during an incident with police near a hotel in West Valley City.\nOfficers with the West Valley City Police Department were called to the Townplace Suites near 5400 West High Market Drive Sunday morning.\nPolice said hotel employees had gone to an outbuilding on the property when they found a \"threatening\" man armed with a metal stick.\nvia KUTVWest Valley CityOctober 25, 2026","source":"web","title":"Ogden seeks to reinvest $2 million in wildfire reimbursements into fire department","url":"https://utah.news/article/1639FECB-1776-45C9-A58E-88949E4AA906"},{"date":"2026-10-21","id":86,"last_updated":"2026-10-25","snippet":"### Suspect fatally shot Sunday morning at West Valley City hotel\nA man was fatally shot by West Valley City Police on Sunday morning at the Towneplace Suites after allegedly threatening hotel staff with a large metal rod.\nWest Valley CityOctober 25, 2026\n...\n### Man killed in police incident after hotel employees found him in West Valley outbuilding\nA man was shot and killed during an incident with police near a hotel in West Valley City.\nOfficers with the West Valley City Police Department were called to the Townplace Suites near 5400 West High Market Drive Sunday morning.\nPolice said hotel employees had gone to an outbuilding on the property when they found a \"threatening\" man armed with a metal stick.\nvia KUTVWest Valley CityOctober 25, 2026","source":"web","title":"Farmington tops Layton 3-0 in 6A girls volleyball","url":"https://utah.news/article/a65a611c-c380-4c46-9188-9d4239aa6e38"},{"id":87,"last_updated":"2026-10-25","snippet":"## SHOOTING\nUPDATED | 2 hours ago\nMan killed in police incident after hotel employees found him in West Valley outbuilding\nA man was shot and killed during an incident with police near a hotel in West Valley City.Officers with the West Valley City Police Department were called to th\n7 hours ago","source":"web","title":"Salt Lake City Topic Shooting | News, Weather, Sports, Breaking News","url":"https://kutv.com/topic/Shooting"},{"date":"2026-10-23","id":88,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"## Grantsville, UT · LATEST NEWS\n### Man dies after being shot by police outside of West Valley City hotel, police say\nWEST VALLEY CITY — A man died after being shot by a police officer outside of a hotel in West Valley City on Sunday morning, police say.\nThe shooting happened outside of Marriott's TownePlace Suites hotel at 5473 West High Market Dr., after hotel employees called to report a man who was found inside a hotel storage building, according to Deputy Communications Director for West Valley City Roxeanne Vainuku.\nWest Valley City, UT · 12h","source":"web","title":"Grantsville, UT Local News and More - NewsBreak","url":"https://www.newsbreak.com/grantsville-ut"},{"date":"2026-10-21","id":89,"last_updated":"2026-10-25","snippet":"### Suspect fatally shot Sunday morning at West Valley City hotel\nA man was fatally shot by West Valley City Police on Sunday morning at the Towneplace Suites after allegedly threatening hotel staff with a large metal rod.\nWest Valley CityOctober 25, 2026\n...\n### Man killed in police incident after hotel employees found him in West Valley outbuilding\nA man was shot and killed during an incident with police near a hotel in West Valley City.\nOfficers with the West Valley City Police Department were called to the Townplace Suites near 5400 West High Market Drive Sunday morning.\nPolice said hotel employees had gone to an outbuilding on the property when they found a \"threatening\" man armed with a metal stick.\nvia KUTVWest Valley CityOctober 25, 2026","source":"web","title":"11 Spartans earn Academic All-State honors in fall sports","url":"https://utah.news/article/77F070C3-D02B-4CED-9534-9AC2032A14A1"},{"id":90,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"# KUTV2news\n- KUTV2news\n@KUTV2News\n5h\nA man was shot and killed during an incident with police near a hotel in West Valley City.\nHotel employees said they called 911 after finding a \"threatening\" man in an outbuilding.\nMan killed in police incident after hotel employees found him in West Valley outbuilding","source":"web","title":"KUTV2News - X","url":"https://x.com/KUTV2News"}],"type":"search_results"},{"queries":["Salt Lake County prosecutors AI review evidence October 26 2026 details","prosecutors conference Salt Lake City AI evidence safeguards October 26 2026"],"results":[{"date":"2026-10-26","id":106,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"# Salt Lake County prosecutors using AI to review evidence; DA says humans remain in control\n10/26/2026 6:20am\nAs prosecutors from across the country gather in Salt Lake City, officials are sharing how artificial intelligence is changing criminal investigations — and why they say safeguards are essential.","source":"web","title":"Browse by Day Archive | 2026/10/26","url":"https://www.ksl.com/archive/2026/10/26/_news_utah_science-and-tech"},{"date":"2026-10-23","id":107,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"Salt Lake County prosecutors using AI to review evidence; DA says humans remain in control | KSL.com\n# Salt Lake County prosecutors using AI to review evidence; DA says humans remain in control\n#### Posted - Oct. 23, 2026 at 4:39 p.m.\n...\n#### Salt Lake County District Attorney Sim Gill provides a walkthrough of the shooting of Carlos Felipe Ocampo-Flores during an availability at his office on April 3. Gill said humans remain in control despite his office using AI to review evidence. (Scott G Winterton, Deseret News)\n...\nKEY TAKEAWAYS\n- Salt Lake County prosecutors are using AI for evidence review, but the maintain human oversight.\n- District Attorney Sim Gill emphasizes how AI aids efficiency without replacing human judgment.\n- The National Prosecution Best Practices Conference is discussing AI's role in the justice system.\nSALT LAKE CITY — Artificial intelligence is already being used inside the Salt Lake County District Attorney's Office, helping prosecutors sort through evidence, conduct legal research and manage growing amounts of digital information.\nBut District Attorney Sim Gill says the technology will not replace the human judgment behind decisions that can change someone's life.\nGill is hosting prosecutors and criminal justice leaders from across the country this week for the 2026 National Prosecution Best Practices Conference, where the responsible use of AI is among several issues being explored.\n\"Certainly the Salt Lake County (District Attorney's Office) is not surrendering its judgment to technology,\" Gill told KSL.\n\"We are not surrendering our human interaction to technology.\"\nThe discussions come as prosecutors nationwide grapple with how to take advantage of increasingly powerful AI tools without compromising sensitive information, introducing errors or allowing machines to influence decisions that should remain in human hands.\nFor Gill, the challenge is finding ways to make his office more efficient while preserving the responsibility prosecutors have to victims, defendants and the communities they serve.\n...\nOne of the biggest challenges facing modern prosecutors is the enormous amount of digital evidence generated during criminal investigations.\nBody-worn cameras, for example, can produce hours of video from a single police response.\nGill described a scenario involving five officers responding to a call lasting 45 minutes.\nEach officer's body camera could generate a separate recording, leaving prosecutors with nearly four hours of video to review.\nAI-assisted technology can help organize that information, produce searchable transcripts and direct attorneys to potentially relevant moments.\nInstead of manually searching every minute of footage for a critical interaction, prosecutors can use technology to identify where to look.\n\"So now I'm going to go put eyes on that myself,\" Gill said, explaining that the technology helps narrow the material requiring closer examination.\n\"It helps me eliminate repetitive, unnecessary work and gets me to the heart of the matter that I need to be looking at.\"\nSalt Lake County District Attorney Sim Gill provides a walkthrough of the shooting of Carlos Felipe Ocampo-Flores during an availability at his office in Salt Lake City on April 3.\nGill said his office is using AI to review evidence, but humans remain in control.\n(Photo: Scott G Winterton, Deseret News)\nGill said his office also uses AI-assisted legal research tools within closed systems rather than open, publicly accessible platforms — an important distinction when handling protected information.\nThe technology can help attorneys locate relevant cases, organize information and examine opposing legal arguments.\nHowever, Gill stressed that prosecutors must still read the source material and independently verify its accuracy.\nHe said the office is not using AI to write court motions or make substantive legal decisions for attorneys.\n...\nBoth district attorneys acknowledged that some of the technology's greatest strengths also introduce significant risks.\nGenerative AI systems can produce inaccurate information or fabricate details, a problem commonly described as an AI \"hallucination.\"\n...\nHe explained that attorneys using AI-assisted legal research tools may receive descriptions of court rulings that do not accurately reflect what a judge decided.\nThat creates an obligation to review the original material rather than relying solely on an AI-generated answer.\n...\nGill raised similar concerns, pointing to instances in the legal profession where attorneys have submitted AI-generated arguments containing references to nonexistent cases.\nHe said his office does not use AI as a substitute for drafting substantive court motions.\n...\nAnother concern is the protection of sensitive information.\nCriminal investigations can involve medical records, criminal histories, witness statements and other material that should not be accessible to unauthorized individuals.\nGill said prosecutors must understand where information goes when uploaded to an AI platform, how it is stored, who owns it and who can retrieve it.\nHolley identified data security as one of his primary concerns, warning against allowing confidential information to enter systems where its protection cannot be assured.\nThe two prosecutors also expressed concern that attorneys could become overly dependent on AI, potentially losing critical skills in research, communication and evaluating people.\n...\nOne issue Gill believes deserves particular attention is the emerging use of AI to help law enforcement officers generate police reports.\nSome technology can turn body-camera recordings into transcripts and use those transcripts to create draft reports.\nGill said he has communicated to law enforcement that officers using such technology should disclose it and personally review the information for accuracy.\n\"What my communication to law enforcement has been is that if you're going to use it, then you need to mention it,\" Gill said.\nHe added that the officer responsible for the report should verify the contents rather than treating an AI-generated draft as a finished account.\n\"I'm not going to put AI technology to testify in court.\nI'm going to put that officer,\" Gill said.\n\"If you're going to use it, let's disclose it.\"\nSalt Lake County District Attorney Sim Gill provides a walkthrough of the shooting of Carlos Felipe Ocampo-Flores during an availability at his office in Salt Lake City on April 3.\nGill provided clear expectations for how he wants AI to be used in his office.\n(Photo: Scott G Winterton, Deseret News)\nGill's comments describe his expectations for disclosure and verification.\nHe did not identify a newly adopted written policy governing AI-generated police reports during the interview.\nHe also emphasized that the district attorney's office would not delegate charging decisions to AI.\nProsecutors must consider whether evidence supports an alleged offense, whether the elements of a crime are met, and whether pursuing charges serves the interests of justice.\nThose decisions require an understanding of the people and circumstances involved, Gill said, rather than a formula producing an automatic recommendation.\nHolley expressed a similar view, rejecting the prospect of AI independently deciding whether charges should be dismissed, a defendant should receive a plea offer or a case should be diverted from prosecution.\n...\nAI could help prosecutors manage those workloads, but it may also require additional software, secure storage, verification procedures and new staff responsibilities.\n...\nThe conversations about AI are only one part of a broader gathering intended to help prosecutors rethink their work.\nThe National Prosecution Best Practices Conference, held Thursday and Friday in Salt Lake City, is co-hosted by the Salt Lake County District Attorney's Office, the Prosecutors' Center for Excellence and its National Best Practices Committee.\nThis year's theme is \"Reimagining the Role of the Prosecutor: Balancing Safety, Prevention, and Public Trust.\"\nGill said the initiative began a decade ago as a way to bring together prosecutors from different jurisdictions and political backgrounds to share research, technology, programs and approaches that could improve the criminal justice system.\nThe gathering includes elected district attorneys and other senior leaders who can take promising ideas back to their communities and potentially implement them through office policies.\n...\nGill also described a conference presentation on AI-generated deepfakes, including technology capable of transforming ordinary images or videos into realistic-looking sexually explicit material.\nHe said those developments demonstrate that prosecutors must consider not only how AI can help them do their jobs, but also how the same technology is creating new challenges for criminal investigations.\n...\nAnd while AI may fundamentally change how attorneys process information, both Gill and Holley believe the most consequential decisions must remain with the people responsible for administering justice.","source":"web","title":"Salt Lake County prosecutors using AI to review evidence; DA says humans remain in control","url":"https://www.ksl.com/article/51640364/salt-lake-county-prosecutors-using-ai-to-review-evidence-da-says-humans-remain-in-control"},{"id":108,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"## Salt Lake County prosecutors using AI to review evidence; DA says humans remain in control\n## As prosecutors from across the country gather in Salt Lake City, officials are sharing how artificial intelligence is changing criminal investigations — and why they say safeguards are essential.\n...\n## Where Salt Lake City, Delta Center and Jazz Bear rank among NBA fans\n- Salt Lake County prosecutors using AI to review evidence; DA says humans remain in control","source":"web","title":"Utah Breaking News, Top Stories \u0026 Sports | World, US, Local","url":"https://www.ksl.com/"},{"date":"2026-02-10","id":109,"last_updated":"2026-10-07","snippet":"Collaborate with prosecutors nationwide and enhance your knowledge of modern criminal justice practices\n2026 National Prosecution Best Practices Conference\nReimagining the Role of the Prosecutor: Balancing Safety, Prevention, and Public Trust\nSalt Lake City, UT\nOctober 22 \u0026 23, 2026\n2026 National Prosecution Best Practices Conference\nSalt Lake City, UT | October 22 \u0026 23, 2026\n...\n# How PCE Can Help\nFrom training prosecutors on topics ranging from artificial intelligence to witness cooperation, providing office assessments, and conducting independent case reviews, PCE has the knowledge base to handle and advise prosecutors on the challenging issues they are facing.\n...\n## Featured PCE Publication\n#### Integrating AI: Guidance and Policies for Prosecutors\nLearn how prosecutors can effectively integrate GAI into their offices.\n...\n## National prosecution BP conference\n#### October 22-23, 2026: Reimagining the Role of the Prosecutor\n#### Independent Case Review","source":"web","title":"Prosecutors' Center for Excellence: Home","url":"https://pceinc.org/"},{"id":110,"last_updated":"2026-10-25","snippet":"## Salt Lake County prosecutors using AI to review evidence; DA says humans remain in control\n#### Eric Cabrera, KSL | Posted Oct. 23 - 4:39 p.m.\n##### As prosecutors from across the country gather in Salt Lake City, officials are sharing how artificial intelligence is changing criminal investigations — and why they say safeguards are essential.","source":"web","title":"Artificial Intelligence | KSL.com","url":"https://www.ksl.com/news/stream/artificial-intelligence-ai-chatgpt"},{"date":"2025-09-23","id":111,"last_updated":"2026-10-08","snippet":"# Prosecutor Training \u0026 Events\n## Upcoming Events\n## NATIONAL PROSECUTION BEST PRACTICES CONFERENCE\n**Reimagining the Role of the Prosecutor: Balancing Safety, Prevention, and Public Trust**\nHosted by PCE, Salt Lake County DA Office and PCE National Best Practices Committee\nLocation: Hilton Salt Lake City Center, Salt Lake City, Utah\nOctober 22-23, 2026","source":"web","title":"Prosecutor Training \u0026 Events","url":"https://pceinc.org/training-and-events/"},{"id":112,"last_updated":"2026-04-14","snippet":"Save the Date: October 2026 National Best\nPractices Conference\n...\nPCE is Studying AI in Prosecution\nProsecutors’ Center for Excellence’s National Best\nPractices’ Committee and Microsoft had a 2-day\nHackathon in Chicago, IL with hands-on learning and experience with Co-Pilot.\nSee PCE’s publication on developing an AI Policy.\nPCE’s AI working group continues the exploration of AI.\nReimagining the role of the\nprosecutor focusing on\ntechnology, juvenile crime, and\nvictims and witnesses.\nPCE is\nteaming up with the Salt Lake\nCounty District Attorney’s\nOffice to host the 4  bi-annual\nNational Best Practices\nConference. \nth\nNATIONAL PROSECUTION BEST\nPRACTICES CONFERENCE\nREIMAGINING THE ROLE OF THE\nPROSECUTOR: BALANCING\nSAFETY, PREVENTION, AND\nPUBLIC TRUST\nSAVE THE DATE\nOCTOBER 22 \u0026 23, 2026\nHilton Salt Lake City Center\nSalt Lake City, Utah\nJoin More than 1,900 Prosecutors\nNationwide for PCE’s AOI Email Series\nAre you receiving PCE’s Articles of\nInterest through a colleague?\nYou can\nsign-up today for the free, weekly email series by filling out a simple request \u003e\nLearn More\nPCE November 2025 Newsletter\nWatch PCE Pop-Ups\nView Past Events\nPCE Trainings\nProsecutors' Center for Excellence\nNEWSLETTER\nThe PCE NBP Committee recently issued two papers on\nProsecuting and Preventing Gun Violence and Police\nImpeachment Disclosure and how they each play a role in prosecutor offices.\n...\nwww.pceinc.org\nRecent topics:\nProsecuting in the Age of AI:\nTools, Ethics, and Strategy \u003e\nScience-Based Interviewing\nfor Detectives and\nProsecutors \u003e","source":"web","title":"[PDF] 2025 Fall Newsletter - Prosecutors' Center for Excellence","url":"https://pceinc.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/2025-Fall-Newsletter-November.pdf"},{"date":"2026-10-16","id":113,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"via Salt Lake TribuneStatewideOctober 26, 2026\n### Salt Lake County prosecutors using AI to review evidence; DA says humans remain in control\nSALT LAKE CITY — Artificial intelligence is already being used inside the Salt Lake County District Attorney's Office, helping prosecutors sort through evidence, conduct legal research and manage growing amounts of digital information.\nBut District Attorney Sim Gill says the technology will not replace the human judgment behind decisions that can change someone's life.\nvia KSLSalt Lake CityOctober 26, 2026","source":"web","title":"Quarterback scores three touchdowns as Bulldogs shut out North Sevier 48-0","url":"https://utah.news/article/56CA814D-741C-4BFD-89BC-5833A53CABFB"},{"date":"2026-07-06","id":114,"last_updated":"2026-09-21","snippet":"# Upcoming Events\n## NATIONAL PROSECUTION BEST PRACTICES CONFERENCE\n**Reimagining the Role of the Prosecutor: Balancing Safety, Prevention, and Public Trust**\nHosted by PCE, Salt Lake County DA Office and PCE National Best Practices Committee\nLocation: Hilton Salt Lake City Center, Salt Lake City, Utah\nOctober 22-23, 2026","source":"web","title":"Upcoming Events - Prosecutors' Center for Excellence","url":"https://pceinc.org/training-and-events/upcoming-events/"},{"date":"2026-10-23","id":115,"last_updated":"2026-10-24","snippet":"# Salt Lake County prosecutors using AI to review evidence; DA says humans remain in control\n10/23/2026 4:39pm\nAs prosecutors from across the country gather in Salt Lake City, officials are sharing how artificial intelligence is changing criminal investigations — and why they say safeguards are essential.","source":"web","title":"Browse by Day Archive | 2026/10/23 | KSL.com","url":"https://www.ksl.com/archive/2026/10/23/_news_utah_police-and-courts"},{"date":"2026-10-23","id":116,"last_updated":"2026-10-25","snippet":"# Salt Lake County prosecutors using AI to review evidence; DA says humans remain in control\n10/23/2026 4:39pm\nAs prosecutors from across the country gather in Salt Lake City, officials are sharing how artificial intelligence is changing criminal investigations — and why they say safeguards are essential.","source":"web","title":"Browse by Day Archive | 2026/10/23","url":"https://www.ksl.com/archive/2026/10/23/_news_utah_science-and-tech"},{"id":117,"last_updated":"2026-10-25","snippet":"# Utah \u0026 U.S. Science \u0026 Technology News\n## Salt Lake County prosecutors using AI to review evidence; DA says humans remain in control\n#### Eric Cabrera, KSL | Posted Oct. 23 - 4:39 p.m. | Save Story\n##### As prosecutors from across the country gather in Salt Lake City, officials are sharing how artificial intelligence is changing criminal investigations — and why they say safeguards are essential.","source":"web","title":"Utah Science News | Tech \u0026 STEM","url":"https://www.ksl.com/news/utah/science-and-tech"},{"id":118,"last_updated":"2026-09-20","snippet":"## About Us\nThank you for your interest in attending the National Best Practices conference on Reimagining the Role of the Prosecutor: Balancing Safety, Prevention, and Public Trust on October 21-23, 2026 in Salt Lake City, Utah.\nPlease join us for this in-person, two-day conference featuring presentations by national speakers and peer guided breakout sessions.\nLunch, breakfast and receptions are included.\nWe will have a welcome reception the evening of Wednesday, October 21st.\nThursday, October 22nd is a full day of programming and discussions with a reception scheduled in the evening.\nFriday, October 23rd includes morning programming and an off-site activity with a reception scheduled for the evening.","source":"web","title":"Reimagining The Role of the Prosecutor: Balancing Safety, ...","url":"https://registration.socio.events/e/reimaginingtheroleoftheprosecutor"},{"date":"2026-10-02","id":119,"last_updated":"2026-10-08","snippet":"No events scheduled for October 26, 2026.\n...\n### Monday, October 26, 2026\nNo events on this day.","source":"web","title":"Archives","url":"https://business.utah.gov/events/category/apex/week/2026-10-26/"},{"date":"2026-03-02","id":120,"last_updated":"2026-10-19","snippet":"# National Best Practices Committee\n### National Best Practices Committee IS Creating a Vision for the Prosecutor Office of the Future\n#### Biennial National Prosecution Best Practices Conference\n##### Co-Hosted By The NBP Committee 2 Conferences In A Row\n2026 National Prosecution Best Practices Conference – Reimagining the Role of the Prosecutor: Balancing Safety, Prevention, and Public Trust\nDate: October 22 and 23, 2026\nLocation: Hilton Salt Lake City Center, Salt Lake City, Utah\nHosts: Salt Lake County DA Office, PCE and PCE NBP\n*Members of the NBP at the 2024 National Prosecution BP Conference*.\n...\n## NBP Publications and Videos\n##### Artificial Intelligence","source":"web","title":"National Best Practices Committee","url":"https://pceinc.org/national-best-practices-committee/"}],"type":"search_results"},{"queries":["Salt Lake City forecast October 26 2026 Monday cold front rain","National Weather Service Salt Lake City October 26 2026 forecast"],"results":[{"date":"2026-10-26","id":91,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"A Pacific storm will bring rain and high elevation snow from the Pacific Northwest into the Northern Rockies.\nA series of storms are expected to move through the Bering Sea bringing strong winds, heavy precipitation, and elevated water levels from the West Coast to northern Alaska.\n...\n## Detailed Forecast\n**Tonight**\nA chance of rain between 9pm and 3am.\nPartly cloudy, with a low around 44.\nSoutheast wind 6 to 11 mph becoming light and variable after midnight.\nChance of precipitation is 30%.\n...\n**Sunday**\nRain likely.\n...\n## ABOUT THIS FORECAST\nLast Update:\n12:31 am MDT Oct 26, 2026\nForecast Valid:\n5am MDT Oct 26, 2026-6pm MST Nov 1, 2026","source":"web","title":"7-Day Forecast 40.75N 111.9W - National Weather Service","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/MapClick.php?textField1=40.76083\u0026textField2=-111.89028"},{"date":"2026-10-26","id":92,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"A Pacific storm will bring rain and high elevation snow from the Pacific Northwest into the Northern Rockies.\nA series of storms are expected to move through the Bering Sea bringing strong winds, heavy precipitation, 