\nSoutheast wind 6 to 11 mph becoming light and variable after midnight.\nChance of precipitation is 30%.\n...\nLast Update:\n12:31 am MDT Oct 26, 2026\nForecast Valid:\n3am MDT Oct 26, 2026-6pm MST Nov 1, 2026","source":"web","title":"7-Day Forecast 40.75N 111.9W","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/MapClick.php?lat=40.758478\u0026lon=-111.888142"},{"date":"2026-10-26","id":95,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"A Pacific storm will bring rain and high elevation snow from the Pacific Northwest into the Northern Rockies.\nA series of storms are expected to move through the Bering Sea bringing strong winds, heavy precipitation, and elevated water levels from the West Coast to northern Alaska.\n...\n**Tonight**\nA slight chance of rain between midnight and 3am.\nPartly cloudy, with a low around 42.\nSouth southeast wind 10 to 15 mph becoming light and variable after midnight.\nWinds could gust as high as 31 mph.\nChance of precipitation is 20%.\n...\nLast Update:\n12:31 am MDT Oct 26, 2026\nForecast Valid:\n5am MDT Oct 26, 2026-6pm MST Nov 1, 2026","source":"web","title":"7-Day Forecast 40.58N 111.87W","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/MapClick.php?lat=40.5725000\u0026lon=-111.8597222"},{"date":"2026-10-26","id":96,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"SALT LAKE CITY (KUTV) — Showers have come to an end across eastern Utah.\nTemperatures will get a big boost heading into Monday.\nThe Wasatch Front will reach the mid-60s with dry skies.\nA cool front will slide through Monday night into Tuesday morning, bringing a few rain showers to northern Utah early Tuesday.\nIt will also drop snow levels in the northern mountains to 7,000 feet, with a dusting to 1 inch possible.","source":"web","title":"Utah warms Monday before cool front brings showers to northern Utah","url":"https://kjzz.com/news/local/utah-warms-monday-before-cool-front-brings-showers-to-northern-utah"},{"date":"2026-10-26","id":97,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"According to the National Weather Service in Salt Lake City, Monday, October 26, will feature mostly sunny skies and a high near 65 degrees.\nSoutheast winds between 5 and 11 mph are expected before rain chances increase overnight.\nA 30% chance of rain develops Monday night, mainly between 9 p.m. and 3 a.m., with temperatures falling to around 44 degrees.","source":"web","title":"Northern Utah Weather: Rain Chances Rise Ahead of Halloween","url":"https://countryherald.com/utah/salt-lake-city/northern-utah-weather-rain-chances-rise-ahead-of-halloween"},{"date":"2026-10-25","id":98,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"2. Monday 26th OctoberMon 26th\nSunny and a moderate breeze\nSunny\nSunny\nHigh18° 65°\nLow8° 46°\nSunny and a moderate breeze","source":"web","title":"Salt Lake City - BBC Weather","url":"https://www.bbc.com/weather/5780993"},{"id":99,"last_updated":"2026-10-25","snippet":"|10/26| | | |61|40|80|1977|37|2020|55|1927|19|2020| |0.90|1982| |5.2|1919| |1|1996| | | | | |","source":"web","title":"Climate - National Weather Service","url":"https://www.weather.gov/wrh/Climate?wfo=slc\u0026tab=cliplot"},{"date":"2026-10-25","id":100,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"## Monday\n18°C 18 degrees Celsius\nSunny\n- Feels like 15°\n- Rain 40% at 10pm\n- Max gust 23mph\n...\n10°C 10 degrees Celsius\nLight rain\n- Feels like 9°\n- Heavy rain 50% at 6am","source":"web","title":"Salt Lake City Int. (United States of America) weather","url":"https://weather.metoffice.gov.uk/forecast/9x0rupcbt?new-design=true"},{"date":"2026-10-26","id":101,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"- A couple of weak storm systems will bring generally light valley\nrain and mountain snow to northern Utah Monday night and Tuesday\nnight.\n- A more substantial storm arrives by the end of the week into the\nweekend with the potential for widespread precipitation that\ncould increase the risk of flash flooding.\n...\nFairly\nbenign weather can be expected into early Monday evening.\nTemperatures on Monday will trend warmer, rising to near to\nslightly above normal across northern Utah but remaining below\nnormal across the south.\nThe upstream trough will end up grazing northern Utah late Monday\nevening through Monday night.\nThis will push a relatively shallow\ncold front into northern Utah.\nA quick round of showers is\nexpected to accompany this front.\n...\nWith snow levels falling as low as\n6500 feet near the Idaho border, some light snow accumulations\ncan be expected over the higher terrain.\n...\nKSLC...VFR conditions are expected to persist through the TAF period\nwith diurnal wind shifts.\nChances for rain begin to increase around\n03z later in the period, though chances at this time remain 20% or\nless.","source":"web","title":"Forecast Discussion","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=slc\u0026issuedby=SLC\u0026product=AFD"},{"date":"2026-10-26","id":102,"last_updated":"2026-10-26","snippet":"140\nFPUS65 KSLC 251843\nSFTUT\nUTZ101\u003e131-WYZ021-261100-\nTabular State Forecast for Utah\nNational Weather Service Salt Lake City UT\n1243 PM MDT SUN OCT 25 2026\nThis product is issued routinely in the early morning and late\nafternoon.\nIt may not represent the latest forecast.\nROWS INCLUDE...\nDaily predominant daytime weather 6AM-6PM\nForecast temperatures...early morning low/daytime high\nProbability of precipitation nighttime 6PM-6AM/daytime 6AM-6PM\n- indicates temperatures below zero\nMM indicates missing data\nFCST FCST FCST FCST FCST FCST FCST\nMon Tue Wed Thu Fri Sat Sun\nOct 26 Oct 27 Oct 28 Oct 29 Oct 30 Oct 31 Nov 01\n...NORTHERN UTAH...\nSalt Lake City\nSunny Ptcldy Ptcldy Ptcldy Rain Rain Mocldy\n41/64 43/59 42/61 45/64 47/60 44/59 42/57\n00/00 40/00 20/10 00/00 30/60 70/60 30/40\nTooele\nSunny Ptcldy Ptcldy Ptcldy Rain Rain Rain\n43/61 43/56 44/57 46/61 48/57 45/56 44/53\n00/00 30/00 20/10 00/00 30/60 60/60 30/60\nOgden\nSunny Sunny Ptcldy Ptcldy Rain Rain Rain\n42/62 44/55 43/57 44/62 47/59 45/57 43/56\n00/00 60/00 20/10 00/00 30/60 80/60 30/